# FluentValidation for TodoApi DTOs Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use `superpowers:subagent-driven-development` (recommended) or `superpowers:executing-plans` to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

## Context

The `TodoApi` project (.NET 8 Web API at `dotnet-interview/TodoApi/`) currently has **no runtime validation** on incoming request payloads. The DTOs `CreateTodoList`, `UpdateTodoList`, `CreateTodoListItem`, and `UpdateTodoListItem` use the C# `required` keyword for compile-time enforcement only — clients can still POST `{"name": ""}` and the controller will happily persist an empty record.

This plan introduces FluentValidation to enforce a `NotEmpty` constraint on `Name` (TodoList DTOs) and `Description` (TodoListItem DTOs). Validation failures are returned to clients as automatic HTTP 400 `ValidationProblemDetails` via the `SharpGrip.FluentValidation.AutoValidation.Mvc` integration package, so the existing controllers stay completely untouched.

**Design decisions (confirmed with user):**
- **Validators target the DTOs**, not the entities. The controllers bind requests to DTOs (`[FromBody] CreateTodoList`, etc.), so this is the layer where validation must run automatically. Putting `IValidator<TodoList>` on the entity would never fire on an HTTP request because the entity is never the action argument.
- **Auto-validation pipeline** via `SharpGrip.FluentValidation.AutoValidation.Mvc` — validation runs as an MVC action filter before the action body executes, returning `ValidationProblemDetails` automatically. No `ModelState` checks are added to controllers.
- **Constraint scope:** `NotEmpty` only on `Name` and `Description`. No `MaximumLength`, no extra `NotNull`.

## Goal

Reject HTTP requests with empty/null `Name` (TodoList create+update) or empty/null `Description` (TodoListItem create+update) with a 400 `ValidationProblemDetails`, without modifying any controller.

## Architecture

- **New folder:** `TodoApi/Validators/` — one `AbstractValidator<T>` per DTO (4 classes total).
- **DI wiring:** `Program.cs` adds `AddFluentValidationAutoValidation()` (filter) and `AddValidatorsFromAssemblyContaining<Program>()` (validator discovery).
- **Failure surface:** auto-validation short-circuits the request and returns 400 `ValidationProblemDetails` before the action runs.
- **Tests:** `TodoApi.Tests/Validators/` — one xUnit test class per validator (3 cases each: null input, empty input, valid input) using `FluentValidation.TestHelper`.

## Tech Stack

- `FluentValidation` 11.9.2
- `FluentValidation.DependencyInjectionExtensions` 11.9.2 (provides `AddValidatorsFromAssemblyContaining`)
- `SharpGrip.FluentValidation.AutoValidation.Mvc` 1.5.0 (MVC filter)
- `FluentValidation.TestHelper` — ships inside the `FluentValidation` package; no separate NuGet ref needed in the test project (transitive via the project reference to TodoApi)

## File Structure

| Action | Path | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| Modify | `dotnet-interview/TodoApi/TodoApi.csproj` | Add 3 `<PackageReference>` entries |
| Modify | `dotnet-interview/TodoApi/Program.cs` | Register validators + auto-validation in DI |
| Create | `dotnet-interview/TodoApi/Validators/CreateTodoListValidator.cs` | `RuleFor(x => x.Name).NotEmpty()` |
| Create | `dotnet-interview/TodoApi/Validators/UpdateTodoListValidator.cs` | `RuleFor(x => x.Name).NotEmpty()` |
| Create | `dotnet-interview/TodoApi/Validators/CreateTodoListItemValidator.cs` | `RuleFor(x => x.Description).NotEmpty()` |
| Create | `dotnet-interview/TodoApi/Validators/UpdateTodoListItemValidator.cs` | `RuleFor(x => x.Description).NotEmpty()` |
| Create | `dotnet-interview/TodoApi.Tests/Validators/CreateTodoListValidatorTests.cs` | xUnit tests, 3 cases |
| Create | `dotnet-interview/TodoApi.Tests/Validators/UpdateTodoListValidatorTests.cs` | xUnit tests, 3 cases |
| Create | `dotnet-interview/TodoApi.Tests/Validators/CreateTodoListItemValidatorTests.cs` | xUnit tests, 3 cases |
| Create | `dotnet-interview/TodoApi.Tests/Validators/UpdateTodoListItemValidatorTests.cs` | xUnit tests, 3 cases |

> All shell commands below assume the working directory is `dotnet-interview/` (where `dotnet-interview.sln` lives).

---

## Tasks

### Task 1: Add NuGet packages

**Files:**
- Modify: `dotnet-interview/TodoApi/TodoApi.csproj`

- [ ] **Step 1: Add three new `<PackageReference>` entries to the existing `<ItemGroup>` in `TodoApi.csproj`**

Insert these three lines inside the existing `<ItemGroup>` that already contains `Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.*` and `Swashbuckle.AspNetCore`:

```xml
<PackageReference Include="FluentValidation" Version="11.9.2" />
<PackageReference Include="FluentValidation.DependencyInjectionExtensions" Version="11.9.2" />
<PackageReference Include="SharpGrip.FluentValidation.AutoValidation.Mvc" Version="1.5.0" />
```

- [ ] **Step 2: Restore packages**

```bash
dotnet restore TodoApi/TodoApi.csproj
```
Expected: completes without errors and downloads the three new packages.

- [ ] **Step 3: Build the API project to confirm it still compiles**

```bash
dotnet build TodoApi/TodoApi.csproj
```
Expected: `Build succeeded. 0 Warning(s) 0 Error(s)`.

- [ ] **Step 4: Commit**

```bash
git add TodoApi/TodoApi.csproj
git commit -m "chore: add FluentValidation packages to TodoApi"
```

---

### Task 2: CreateTodoListValidator (TDD)

**Files:**
- Test: `dotnet-interview/TodoApi.Tests/Validators/CreateTodoListValidatorTests.cs`
- Create: `dotnet-interview/TodoApi/Validators/CreateTodoListValidator.cs`

- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**

Create `dotnet-interview/TodoApi.Tests/Validators/CreateTodoListValidatorTests.cs`:

```csharp
using FluentValidation.TestHelper;
using TodoApi.Dtos;
using TodoApi.Validators;

namespace TodoApi.Tests.Validators;

public class CreateTodoListValidatorTests
{
    private readonly CreateTodoListValidator _validator = new();

    [Fact]
    public void Should_have_error_when_Name_is_null()
    {
        var model = new CreateTodoList { Name = null! };
        var result = _validator.TestValidate(model);
        result.ShouldHaveValidationErrorFor(x => x.Name);
    }

    [Fact]
    public void Should_have_error_when_Name_is_empty()
    {
        var model = new CreateTodoList { Name = string.Empty };
        var result = _validator.TestValidate(model);
        result.ShouldHaveValidationErrorFor(x => x.Name);
    }

    [Fact]
    public void Should_not_have_error_when_Name_is_provided()
    {
        var model = new CreateTodoList { Name = "Groceries" };
        var result = _validator.TestValidate(model);
        result.ShouldNotHaveValidationErrorFor(x => x.Name);
    }
}
```

- [ ] **Step 2: Run the test to verify it fails**

```bash
dotnet test TodoApi.Tests/TodoApi.Tests.csproj --filter "FullyQualifiedName~CreateTodoListValidatorTests"
```
Expected: build error — `CS0234: The type or namespace name 'Validators' does not exist in the namespace 'TodoApi'`. (Failing-to-compile counts as a failing test in TDD red.)

- [ ] **Step 3: Create the validator**

Create `dotnet-interview/TodoApi/Validators/CreateTodoListValidator.cs`:

```csharp
using FluentValidation;
using TodoApi.Dtos;

namespace TodoApi.Validators;

public class CreateTodoListValidator : AbstractValidator<CreateTodoList>
{
    public CreateTodoListValidator()
    {
        RuleFor(x => x.Name).NotEmpty();
    }
}
```

- [ ] **Step 4: Run the test to verify it passes**

```bash
dotnet test TodoApi.Tests/TodoApi.Tests.csproj --filter "FullyQualifiedName~CreateTodoListValidatorTests"
```
Expected: `Passed: 3, Failed: 0`.

- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**

```bash
git add TodoApi/Validators/CreateTodoListValidator.cs TodoApi.Tests/Validators/CreateTodoListValidatorTests.cs
git commit -m "feat: add CreateTodoListValidator with NotEmpty rule on Name"
```

