# FluentValidation for TodoApi DTOs Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use `superpowers:subagent-driven-development` (recommended) or `superpowers:executing-plans` to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

## Context

The `TodoApi` project (.NET 8 Web API at `dotnet-interview/TodoApi/`) currently has **no runtime validation** on incoming request payloads. The DTOs `CreateTodoList`, `UpdateTodoList`, `CreateTodoListItem`, and `UpdateTodoListItem` use the C# `required` keyword for compile-time enforcement only — clients can still POST `{"name": ""}` and the controller will happily persist an empty record.

This plan introduces FluentValidation to enforce a `NotEmpty` constraint on `Name` (TodoList DTOs) and `Description` (TodoListItem DTOs). Validation failures are returned to clients as automatic HTTP 400 `ValidationProblemDetails` via the `SharpGrip.FluentValidation.AutoValidation.Mvc` integration package, so the existing controllers stay completely untouched.

**Design decisions (confirmed with user):**
- **Validators target the DTOs**, not the entities. The controllers bind requests to DTOs (`[FromBody] CreateTodoList`, etc.), so this is the layer where validation must run automatically. Putting `IValidator<TodoList>` on the entity would never fire on an HTTP request because the entity is never the action argument.
- **Auto-validation pipeline** via `SharpGrip.FluentValidation.AutoValidation.Mvc` — validation runs as an MVC action filter before the action body executes, returning `ValidationProblemDetails` automatically. No `ModelState` checks are added to controllers.
- **Constraint scope:** `NotEmpty` only on `Name` and `Description`. No `MaximumLength`, no extra `NotNull`.

## Goal

Reject HTTP requests with empty/null `Name` (TodoList create+update) or empty/null `Description` (TodoListItem create+update) with a 400 `ValidationProblemDetails`, without modifying any controller.

## Architecture

- **New folder:** `TodoApi/Validators/` — one `AbstractValidator<T>` per DTO (4 classes total).
- **DI wiring:** `Program.cs` adds `AddFluentValidationAutoValidation()` (filter) and `AddValidatorsFromAssemblyContaining<Program>()` (validator discovery).
- **Failure surface:** auto-validation short-circuits the request and returns 400 `ValidationProblemDetails` before the action runs.
- **Tests:** `TodoApi.Tests/Validators/` — one xUnit test class per validator (3 cases each: null input, empty input, valid input) using `FluentValidation.TestHelper`.

## Tech Stack

- `FluentValidation` 11.9.2
- `FluentValidation.DependencyInjectionExtensions` 11.9.2 (provides `AddValidatorsFromAssemblyContaining`)
- `SharpGrip.FluentValidation.AutoValidation.Mvc` 1.5.0 (MVC filter)
- `FluentValidation.TestHelper` — ships inside the `FluentValidation` package; no separate NuGet ref needed in the test project (transitive via the project reference to TodoApi)

